## Coding Standards

- **Simplicity:** minimal code; stdlib over deps; delete over add; no one-impl interfaces / one-product factories / unused config.
- **Naming:** descriptive; booleans `is`/`has`/`should`; handlers `handle*`/`on*`; acronyms `userId`/`apiUrl` (`IO` stays upper); files kebab-case; components PascalCase.
- **Structure:** group by feature; one export per file (unless tight helpers); barrels for public API only; tests co-located (`*.test.ts`).
- **Functions:** one job; max ~20 lines; early returns; pure over globals - pass deps in.
- **Errors:** never swallow; typed over strings; handle at boundary; message = what failed + what to do.
- **Types:** no `any` (narrow `unknown`); `interface` for public APIs; readonly by default; exhaustive switches.
- **Tests:** behavior not impl; one `describe`/feature, one `it`/behavior; AAA; no shared mutable state across tests.
- **Comments:** WHY only; no mission/plan/draft provenance in source; no commented-out dead code; `TODO(#n): …` only; delete restating noise.
- **Console:** no `console.log` in prod; `console.error` / `console.warn` only when warranted.
